ter"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.lem-odometer"],"id":"long.lem-odometer","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Lemma 11.2 (Divisor-residue form of the short-window phase)","locator":"Long record Lemma 11.2, p. 122, label lem:odometer","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*For all $M,L\\ge 1$,\n$$\n\\Theta_L(M)\\ =\\ \\sum_{d\\ge 2}\\ \\sum_{\\substack{1\\le i\\le L\\\\ i\\,\\equiv\\,-M\\ (\\mathrm{mod}\\ d)}} 2^{-i}\n\\ =\\ \\sum_{d\\ge 2}\\ 2^{-i_d(M)}\\cdot\\frac{1-2^{-d\\,m_d}}{1-2^{-d}},\n$$\nwhere $i_d(M)\\in[1,d]$ is the least $i\\ge1$ with $d\\mid M+i$ (so $i_d(M)$ depends only on $M \\bmod d$), $m_d := \\#\\{1\\le i\\le L: d\\mid M+i\\}$, and terms with $i_d(M)>L$ are empty. In particular, for every integer $D\\ge M+L$,\n$$\n\\Theta_L(M)\\ =\\ \\sum_{d=2}^{D}\\ \\sum_{i=1}^{L} 2^{-i}\\,\\mathbf 1_{d\\mid M+i},\n$$\nand the right-hand side, with an arbitrary integer $x\\ge0$ in place of $M$, depends on $x$ only through its residues modulo the integers $d$ with $2\\le d\\le D$. The cutoff $D$ has to be fixed before the argument varies: at $(M,L)=(1,1)$ the cutoff is $M+L=2$, the integers $1$ and $3$ have the same residue modulo every $d$ with $2\\le d\\le 2$, and yet $\\Theta_1(1)=1/2$ while $\\Theta_1(3)=1$.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.lem-odometer","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.lem-odometer","id":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.lem-odometer%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.ShortWindowDivisorPhase.Psi_eq_of_residues_eq%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.lem-odometer%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.ShortWindowDivisorPhase.Psi_eq_of_residues_eq%22%2C%